SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Versión estenográfica. Conferencia de prensa del presidente Andrés Manuel López Obrador del 1 de junio de 2022","publisher":"Presidencia de la República 2018-2024 | Gobierno | gob.mx","publication_date":"2022-06-01","url":"https://www.gob.mx/amlo/articulos/version-estenografica-conferencia-de-prensa-del-presidente-andres-manuel-lopez-obrador-del-1-de-junio-de-2022","claim":"AMLO said the prior year's income was about 1.6 million pesos, that current-year income still had to be reported, that Beatriz manages his income, and that he has no material possessions.","locator":"Q&A on declaration patrimonial / ingresos","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous presidential transcript with direct first-person statements; self-report, but precise and attributable.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to his personal-finance disclosure.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own public statement, but the claims are self-reported and not independently audited in the transcript.","contrary_evidence":["Self-reporting is not independent verification and does not exclude omissions or opaque income routing."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Reporta López Obrador ingresos por 1.71 millones de pesos en 2022","publisher":"Excélsior","publication_date":"2023-05-27","url":"https://www.excelsior.com.mx/nacional/reporta-lopez-obrador-ingresos-por-171-millones-de-pesos-en-2022/1589209","claim":"The president's 2022 patrimonial declaration reported 1,697,081 pesos of salary plus a 19,310-peso adult-pension benefit, and it said he had no vehicles or properties in his name.","locator":"lead paragraph / declaration summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific reporting on a filed declaration with precise numbers, though still mediated by the newspaper.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective report on a 2022 declaration filed in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own filed declaration, with the limitation that declarations can omit spouse-held assets and some forms of income.","contrary_evidence":["The filing is self-reported and cannot by itself rule out spouse-held or undisclosed interests."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"AMLO reconoce que proceso de “donativo” de la FGR para rifa fue incorrecto; regresó 2 mil mdp al Infonavit","publisher":"Animal Político","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://animalpolitico.com/2022/02/amlo-proceso-donativo-rifa-avion-incorrecto-regreso-dinero-infonavit","claim":"AMLO said the 2 billion pesos from the FGR's 'donative' for the presidential raffle had been returned to Infonavit because the original procedure was legally incorrect, and he framed the correction as a use of the money for housing credits for poor families.","locator":"presidential quote in article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of a direct admission and correction, but it concerns an institutional transaction rather than a personal-finance disclosure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's admission of an institutional error and subsequent correction.","contrary_evidence":["The episode concerns a state-funds procedure rather than clear personal wrongdoing."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"AMLO enviará a la FGR declaración por escrito por el caso de su hermano Pío; ‘no tengo nada de qué avergonzarme’, dice","publisher":"Animal Político","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://animalpolitico.com/2022/08/amlo-declaracion-escrito-fiscalia-hermano-pio-lopez-morena","claim":"AMLO said he would not appear in person but would send a written statement to the FGR about the investigation into his brother Pío's alleged campaign financing, and he said he had nothing to be ashamed of and that all information should be delivered to the INE.","locator":"article body / direct quote","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct quote in contemporaneous reporting about his response to scrutiny of a close family member.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's response to scrutiny involving a close family member; it shows willingness to engage, though the underlying allegations were about his brother, not his own assets.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying allegation concerned his brother's conduct, so this is indirect rather than proof about AMLO's own finances."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"La Fiscalía abre una investigación por el caso del hijo de López Obrador y un contratista de Pemex","publisher":"EL PAÍS México","publication_date":"2022-02-22","url":"https://elpais.com/mexico/2022-02-22/la-fiscalia-abre-una-investigacion-por-el-caso-del-hijo-de-lopez-obrador-y-un-contratista-de-pemex.html","claim":"After the Baker Hughes/house controversy prompted a FGR investigation, AMLO said there was no problem if complaints were filed against his son or his son's spouse and that they should be processed, adding that everyone should answer to the authority.","locator":"article body / quoted presidential response","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report of a direct presidential response to a family-related conflict-of-interest allegation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's response to scrutiny of a close family member; it suggests tolerance of investigation but does not resolve the underlying conflict allegation.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying Baker Hughes matter remained contested, and the article itself notes the allegation was still under investigation."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"El Instituto de Transparencia rechaza la solicitud de López Obrador para investigar los ingresos de Loret de Mola","publisher":"EL PAÍS México","publication_date":"2022-02-16","url":"https://elpais.com/mexico/2022-02-16/el-instituto-de-transparencia-rechaza-la-solicitud-de-lopez-obrador-para-investigar-los-ingresos-de-loret-de-mola.html","claim":"AMLO asked the INAI to determine the origin of Carlos Loret de Mola's wealth and make his income and assets public, but the INAI said it had no constitutional or legal authority to carry out that kind of investigation.","locator":"article body / INAI response","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous report on a formal presidential request and the independent body's legal rejection.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's use of a transparency body against a critic; the response shows the request exceeded INAI authority.","contrary_evidence":["The president framed the request as transparency, but the target was a journalist critical of his government."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gasolina, inflación y apoyos sociales: los dichos de AMLO en Dos Bocas","publisher":"Animal Político","publication_date":"2022-07-02","url":"https://animalpolitico.com/verificacion-de-hechos/fact-checking/gasolina-inflacion-y-apoyos-sociales-dichos-de-amlo-dos-bocas?rtbref=rtb_5dfl4sjvxtihya96b6rn_1714385558325","claim":"The fact-check found false or misleading AMLO claims in his Dos Bocas speech, including his statement that 80% of Mexican households receive some budget support without intermediaries; the article says official data put the share at 34% in early 2022.","locator":"section on 'apoyos sociales' / 80% households claim","source_type":"media/fact-check","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed fact-check with official data cross-checking and a clear verdict on a specific claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about a 2022 presidential speech.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own public statement; the falsity concerns a speech, not a policy filing.","contrary_evidence":["The same article says some other parts of the Dos Bocas speech were true, so the negative applies only to the specific 80% claim."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"López Obrador sobre el 'caso Ayotzinapa': 'Encinas es un hombre íntegro. Hay pruebas suficientes y se van a ir reforzando'","publisher":"EL PAÍS México","publication_date":"2022-11-01","url":"https://elpais.com/mexico/2022-11-01/lopez-obrador-sobre-el-caso-ayotzinapa-encinas-es-un-hombre-integro-hay-pruebas-suficientes-y-se-van-a-ir-reforzando.html","claim":"After the GIEI said it could not verify all the screenshots used by the government's Ayotzinapa commission and some appeared false, AMLO responded that the elements were solid, there were enough proofs, and the investigation would be strengthened.","locator":"article body / quoted exchange on GIEI findings","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting on a specific dispute where later evidence undermined parts of the government's presentation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's response to an integrity-sensitive government investigation; the disputed evidence was not fully validated.","contrary_evidence":["The case involved a government commission and unresolved criminal investigation, so some caution is warranted about treating every disputed element as deliberate falsehood."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across presidential transcripts, INAI and FGR-related coverage, Baker Hughes and Pío family-allegation reporting, fact-checking pieces on AMLO speeches, and broader press-freedom context. I kept 14 distinct URLs in the dossier, with the reused items covering the repeated anti-press / truthfulness pattern and the new items covering personal-finance disclosure, family-scrutiny responses, a correction after an incorrect state-funds procedure, and specific false or misleading 2022 claims. I rejected broader corruption indices, generic press-freedom summaries, and 2023-2025 fact checks unless they directly bore on a 2022 AMLO statement or a 2022 filed declaration. I also rejected items that only described Mexico's inherited corruption environment without a ruler-specific personal-nexus claim.

Remaining gaps
- I did not find a conclusive 2022 finding of personal enrichment, bribery, or hidden ownership directly attributable to AMLO himself.
- The strongest family-conflict episode, Baker Hughes/José Ramón, remained contested and did not produce an independent finding of self-dealing by AMLO.
- Evidence on appointments, loyalists, and transactional favoritism is thinner than the evidence on public truthfulness and media attacks.
- More search would help on 7B.3, 7B.4, 7B.5, and 7B.9, especially if you want stronger documentary proof on contracts, beneficial ownership, or appointment patterns tied to close associates.
